%% Retrieval keeps Qdrant structural metadata while hydrating canonical content from PostgreSQL.

flowchart TD
    A([User query])
    B{Greeting or blank?}
    C[Return greeting or empty result<br/>without retrieval]
    D{Needs clarification?}
    E[Ask clarification<br/>without retrieval]
    F[Complete or rewrite query<br/>from conversation context]
    G[Prepare dense + sparse query]
    H[Apply shared hard filters]
    I[Hard filters<br/>approved + published + student audience]
    J[(Qdrant dense candidates<br/>score + structural payload)]
    K[(PostgreSQL FTS/BM25 candidates)]
    L[Fetch Qdrant payload for<br/>sparse-only candidates by point id]
    LA[RRF or weighted fusion]
    M[Hydrate fused canonical content<br/>from PostgreSQL; keep Qdrant metadata]
    N[Rerank fused candidates]
    O[Structural expansion]
    P[Hit child item<br/>add logical parent]
    Q[Hit parent item + list query<br/>add direct children]
    R[List-intent query<br/>optionally add siblings]
    S[Hit split<br/>add related split neighbors]
    T[Deduplicate by chunk_key]
    U[Sort by source order]
    V[Apply context budget]
    W[Build citations from canonical content<br/>and page ranges]
    X([RetrievalResult])

    A --> B
    B -->|yes| C
    B -->|no| D
    D -->|yes| E
    D -->|no| F --> G --> H
    I --> H
    H --> J
    H --> K
    J --> LA
    K --> L --> LA
    LA --> M --> N --> O
    O --> P
    O --> Q
    O --> R
    O --> S
    P --> T
    Q --> T
    R --> T
    S --> T
    T --> U --> V --> W --> X

    J -. metadata retained .-> Y[logical_item_key + logical_item_keys<br/>parent_item_key<br/>logical_table_key + logical_code_key<br/>split_index + split_count<br/>chunk_index/source_order<br/>heading_path + item_path<br/>item_marker + item_level<br/>block_type + legal_unit_type]
    K -. sparse score + qdrant_point_id .-> L
    M -. PostgreSQL is canonical content source .-> N
    Z{{Do not expand entire Parent<br/>when one item branch is enough}} -. budget rule .-> V
